  "notes": [
    "The Billion Year Countdown - English SF novel, ~46,800 words of running prose, the single best item here: long, English, pure narrative, no quotation and no boilerplate. Date: docx dcterms:created 2016-10-28T16:05, dcterms:modified 2018-08-05T15:50, cp:revision 1947; the sibling PDF carries creationDate D:20180805 with producer PDFCreator 3.1.2 and iTextSharp 5.5.12, both 2017/2018-era builds. Self-published via Lulu alongside the Ringe des Lebens trilogy. DMS CRE-005.",
    "8PWC.hardcover.en - Eight Pattern Wing Chun Kuen, ~29,500 words of running prose. Date: docx modified 2011-06-13T22:00; title page reads 'by Matthias Gruber' and '(c) 2011 Matthias Gruber. All rights reserved. ISBN: 978-1-4476-7964-6', which is a published and verifiable record. Original English, not a translation: the EN docx was finished 2011-06-13 and the DE 2011-09-24, both branched from one template on 2011-05-30.",
    "8PWCS - Eight Pattern Wing Chun, Safety and Security, ~22,800 words of running prose; the cleanest expository English here after the novel. Date: docx dcterms:created 2012-06-09T14:34, modified 2013-12-24T00:13, dc:creator 'Matthias Gruber'; the text opens '(c) 2012 Matthias Gruber'. Unpublished manuscript.",
    "DO NOT ADD the 2nd-edition 8PWC docx alongside the 1st. Measured: 909 body paragraphs each, 29,514 vs 29,523 running-prose words - it is the same text. Word's higher 53,425 figure for the 2nd edition is text-box and table content outside the body flow. Pooling both scores the same sentences twice and the resulting flag rate is fiction.",
    "DO NOT source any of this from ~/scifi/manuscripts/ or ~/scifi/translations/. That repository's own git log records 'BYC English polish pass', 'structural edit' and subagent-produced files - it is LLM-edited, in both languages.",
    "Resolution floor: at the 320-word default this is roughly 310 chunks, so the smallest flag rate it can resolve is about 0.3%. The published Binoculars low-FPR threshold was chosen at 0.01% FPR, which no corpus of this size can confirm - report what is resolvable, not what is quoted."
  ],
